		Intel X86 BSP

Table of Contents
=================

	1. Supported Boards
	2. Change History
	3. BSP Notes

1. Supported Boards
===================

This BSP supports the following boards:

	+ Intel Ice Lake-SP: 3rd Gen Intel(R) Xeon(R) Scalable processor
	+ Intel Idaville LCC: Intel Xeon D Processors, Ice Lake-D SoC, (IOTG: Brighton City)
	+ Intel Idaville HCC: Intel Xeon D Processors, Ice Lake-D SoC, (Moro City)
	+ Intel Sapphire Rapids: Intel Xeon(R) Platinum 8468H
	+ Intel Harcuvar platform: Atom Processor, Denverton-NS SoC, (Harcuvar)
	+ Intel Meteor Lake H: Intel(R) Core(TM) Ultra 7 155H processors
	+ Intel Arrow Lake S: Intel(R) Core(TM) Ultra 7 265K processors

2. Change History
=================

	- 2025/09 (LINUXPG-2689) Add Arrow Lake S support
	- 2025/09 (LINUXPG-2690) Add Meteor Lake H support
	- 2025/09 (LINUXPG-2590) Add Denverton-NS support
	- 2025/09 (LINUXPG-2593) Add Sapphire Rapids support
	- 2025/09 (LINUXPG-2591) Add Icelake-D support
	- 2025/05 (LINUXPG-2592) Add Ice Lake-SP support

3. BSP Notes
============

This BSP has been validated exclusively for the boards listed in the following
'Validated Board Info' sections. Using it with other hardware configurations may
result in compatibility issues.

3.1 Intel Ice Lake-SP
---------------------

Ice Lake-SP is Intel's 3rd Generation of Xeon Scalable Processors which is
built on 10nm process, as the successor to Cascade Lake-SP.

3.1.1 Validated Board Info
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

[BIOS info]
	Vendor: Intel Corporation
	Version: SE5C6200.86B.4018.D65.2010201151
	Release Date: 10/20/2020

[Processor Info]
	Cpu family      : 6
	Model           : 106
	Model name      : Intel(R) Xeon(R) Platinum 8360Y CPU
	Stepping        : 6

[Board info]
	 Intel Server System M50CYP Family

3.1.2 Supported Features
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

	o Bus
		+ PCI Express 4.0
		+ I2C/SMBus: Intel Corporation C620 Series Chipset Family SMBus [8086:a1a3] (rev 0a)

	o Network
		+ Gb Ethernet: Intel Corporation I210 Gigabit Network Connection [8086:1533] (rev 03)
		+ 10Gb Ethernet: Intel Corporation Ethernet Controller 10G X550T [8086:1563] (rev 01)

	o USB
		+ USB 3.0 Host: Intel Corporation C620 Series Chipset Family USB 3.0 xHCI Controller [8086:a1af] (rev 0a)

	o Storage
		+ SATA3: Intel Corporation C620 Series Chipset Family SATA Controller [AHCI mode] [8086:a182] (rev 0a)

	o Multimedia
		+ Graphics: ASPEED Technology, Inc. ASPEED Graphics Family [1a03:2000] (rev 41)

	o Power Management
		+ CPU Freq: ACPI P-state
		+ CPU Idle: ACPI C-state
		+ ACPI S0
		+ ACPI S4

	o Misc Devices
		+ RTC: PC-style CMOS RTC
		+ Input device
			+ USB mouse & keyboard
		+ HW Monitor: Intel CPU core temperature sensor

	o NUMA (Non-Uniform Memory Access)

	o TPM2.0

	o EDAC

	o Intel QuickAssit Technology
		 + Intel (R) QuickAssist Adapter 8970

	o Intel Optane Persistent Memory 200 Series Module (Code name: Barlow Pass)

3.1.3 Unsupported Features
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The following features are not supported and not validated.

	x Hardware Watchdog
	x ACPI S3

1) You can see the following log during kernel booting.

    iTCO_wdt: unable to reset NO_REBOOT flag, device disabled by hardware/BIOS.

This means the watchdog is disabled by HW/BIOS, and thus not usable.

2) ACPI S3 is not supported by BIOS.

3.1.4 Note
~~~~~~~~~~

The default serial console port is ttyS1 at I/O 0x2f8. It may be different on your board
due to different hardware or BIOS settings.

3.1.5 Known Issue
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

A kernel NULL pointer dereference may occur during system hibernation (suspend-to-disk),
triggered by the Linux ice driver, with the following call trace in log.

    BUG: kernel NULL pointer dereference, address: 0000000000000048
    #PF: supervisor read access in kernel mode
    #PF: error_code(0x0000) - not-present page
    PGD 0
    Oops: Oops: 0000 [#1] PREEMPT_RT SMP NOPTI

    Call Trace:
     <TASK>
     ice_vsi_set_napi_queues+0x4f/0xe0 [ice]
     ice_resume+0xf4/0x220 [ice]
     pci_pm_thaw+0x48/0xa0
     ? __pfx_pci_pm_thaw+0x10/0x10
     dpm_run_callback+0x47/0x160
     device_resume+0xb8/0x1f0
     async_resume+0x21/0x40
     async_run_entry_fn+0x2d/0xb0
     process_one_work+0x156/0x340
     worker_thread+0x34a/0x480
     ? __pfx_worker_thread+0x10/0x10
     kthread+0xf7/0x120
     ? __pfx_kthread+0x10/0x10
     ret_from_fork+0x3e/0x60
     ? __pfx_kthread+0x10/0x10
     ret_from_fork_asm+0x1a/0x30
     </TASK>

No upstream fix is currently available. To mitigate this issue, unload the ice driver
module using "modprobe -r ice" before initiating suspend-to-disk, then reload it with
"modprobe ice" after system resume.

