4. Common Known Issues
======================

1) Engineer Samples of Intel Ethernet Adapter sometimes don't have valid MAC addresses, like

    root@intel-x86-64:~# ifconfig | grep ether
            ether 00:00:00:00:01:00
            ether 00:00:00:00:01:01
            ether 00:00:00:00:01:02
            ether 00:00:00:00:01:03

Before performing network testing, ensure that valid MAC addresses are assigned to each interface.

2) When configuring kdump, ensure the dump-capture kernel uses intel_iommu=off with the e1000e driver.
Otherwise, the following error may occur:

    e1000e 0000:80:1f.6 eth0: Detected Hardware Unit Hang:
      TDH                  <0>
      TDT                  <1>
      next_to_use          <1>
      next_to_clean        <0>
    buffer_info[next_to_clean]:
      time_stamp           <100260e30>
      next_to_watch        <0>
      jiffies              <10026e400>
      next_to_watch.status <0>
    MAC Status             <40080083>
    PHY Status             <796d>
    PHY 1000BASE-T Status  <3800>
    PHY Extended Status    <3000>
    PCI Status             <10>

3) In dump-capture kernel, you may see the following call trace.

    thunderbolt 0000:00:0d.2: interrupt for RX ring 0 is already disabled
    WARNING: CPU: 8 PID: 177 at /drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.c:146 ring_interrupt_active+0x257/0x2b0 [thunderbolt]
    Call Trace:
     <TASK>
     ? __pfx_pci_pm_runtime_suspend+0x10/0x10
     tb_ring_stop+0xda/0x190 [thunderbolt]
     tb_ctl_stop+0x40/0xb0 [thunderbolt]
     tb_domain_runtime_suspend+0x36/0x50 [thunderbolt]
     nhi_runtime_suspend+0x23/0x50 [thunderbolt]
     pci_pm_runtime_suspend+0x62/0x150
     __rpm_callback+0x49/0x160
     ? __pfx_pci_pm_runtime_suspend+0x10/0x10
     rpm_callback+0x60/0x70
     ? __pfx_pci_pm_runtime_suspend+0x10/0x10
     rpm_suspend+0xeb/0x610
     ? __pfx_pci_pm_runtime_idle+0x10/0x10
     rpm_idle+0x278/0x3e0
     pm_runtime_work+0x97/0xd0
     process_one_work+0x153/0x320
     worker_thread+0x32a/0x460
     ? __pfx_worker_thread+0x10/0x10
     kthread+0xe5/0x120
     ? __pfx_kthread+0x10/0x10
     ret_from_fork+0x3e/0x60
     ? __pfx_kthread+0x10/0x10
     ret_from_fork_asm+0x1a/0x30
     </TASK>

To avoid it, use "module_blacklist=thunderbolt" with the capture kernel.

4) PMEM DAX (direct access to persistent memory) is not supported on RT kernel.
Because DEV_DAX_PMEM has the following dependencies.

    DEV_DAX_PMEM depends on LIBNVDIMM && NVDIMM_DAX && DEV_DAX
    DEV_DAX depends on TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE
    TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE depends on HAVE_ARCH_TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE && !PREEMPT_RT_FULL
